1
00:00:00,840 --> 00:00:05,079
this time, as before, make use of the fallen stones.

2
00:00:05,079 --> 00:00:07,719
This time the stones had vanished, too.

3
00:00:07,719 --> 00:00:12,440
The force of the explosion had flung them to distances of hundreds of yards.

4
00:00:12,440 --> 00:00:16,520
It was as though the windmill had never been.

5
00:00:16,520 --> 00:00:21,120
As they approached the farm, Squealer, who had unaccountably been absent during

6
00:00:21,120 --> 00:00:27,760
the fighting, came skipping towards them, whisking his tail, and beaming with satisfaction.

7
00:00:27,760 --> 00:00:35,719
And the animals heard, from the direction of the farm buildings, the solemn booming of a gun.

8
00:00:36,680 --> 00:00:39,239
"What is that gun firing for?"

9
00:00:39,239 --> 00:00:40,879
said Boxer.

10
00:00:40,879 --> 00:00:43,479
"To celebrate our victory!"

11
00:00:43,479 --> 00:00:45,120
cried Squealer.

12
00:00:45,120 --> 00:00:46,799
"What victory?"

13
00:00:46,799 --> 00:00:48,239
said Boxer.

14
00:00:48,239 --> 00:00:53,239
His knees were bleeding. He had lost a shoe and split his hoof, and a dozen

15
00:00:53,239 --> 00:00:56,479
pellets had lodged themselves in his hind leg.

16
00:00:56,479 --> 00:01:00,719
"What victory, comrade? Have we not driven the enemy off our soil, the

17
00:01:00,719 --> 00:01:05,000
sacred soil of Animal Farm?"

18
00:01:05,200 --> 00:01:07,559
"But they have destroyed the windmill.

19
00:01:07,559 --> 00:01:10,440
And we had worked on it for two years."

20
00:01:10,440 --> 00:01:15,040
"What matter? We will build another windmill. We will build six windmills if

21
00:01:15,040 --> 00:01:19,959
we feel like it. You do not appreciate, comrade, the mighty thing that we have

22
00:01:19,959 --> 00:01:25,440
done. The enemy was in occupation of this very ground that we stand upon, and

23
00:01:25,440 --> 00:01:33,959
now, thanks to the leadership of Comrade Napoleon, we have won every inch of it back again.

24
00:01:34,120 --> 00:01:37,520
>> Then we have won back what we had before.

25
00:01:37,520 --> 00:01:39,840
>> That is our victory.

26
00:01:39,840 --> 00:01:42,280
>> They limped into the yard.

27
00:01:42,280 --> 00:01:46,719
The pellets under the skin of Boxer's leg smarted painfully.

28
00:01:46,719 --> 00:01:51,959
He saw ahead of him the heavy labor of rebuilding the windmill from the foundations.

29
00:01:51,959 --> 00:01:57,040
And already, in imagination, he braced himself for the task.

30
00:01:57,040 --> 00:02:02,120
But for the first time, it occurred to him that he was 11 years old,

31
00:02:02,120 --> 00:02:06,920
and that perhaps his great muscles were not quite what they had once been.

32
00:02:06,920 --> 00:02:12,000
But when the animals saw the green flag flying, and heard the gun firing again,

33
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:17,520
seven times it was fired in all, and heard the speech that Napoleon made

34
00:02:17,520 --> 00:02:22,639
congratulating them on their conduct, it did seem to them, after all, that they

35
00:02:22,639 --> 00:02:25,680
had won a great victory.

36
00:02:25,680 --> 00:02:29,600
The animals slain in the battle were given a solemn funeral.

37
00:02:29,600 --> 00:02:34,799
Boxer and Clover pulled the wagon which served as a hearse, and Napoleon himself

38
00:02:34,799 --> 00:02:37,360
walked at the head of the procession.

39
00:02:37,360 --> 00:02:40,799
Two whole days were given over to celebrations.

40
00:02:40,799 --> 00:02:45,920
There were songs, speeches, and more firing of the gun, and a special gift of

41
00:02:45,920 --> 00:02:51,879
an apple was bestowed on every animal, with 2 oz of corn for each bird, and

42
00:02:51,879 --> 00:02:54,840
three biscuits for each dog.

43
00:02:54,840 --> 00:02:59,799
It was announced that the battle would be called the Battle of the Windmill,

44
00:02:59,799 --> 00:03:00,000
and that Napoleon had created a new
